<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore bunkers down, 380-cst at $104-$105/T.</title>
<headline>Singapore bunkers down, 380-cst at $104-$105/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore bunker prices were weaker, with majors seen undercutting each other, indicating very low offers, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>A major was offering bunker 380-cst at $104-$105 per tonne after selling a 600 tonne parcel at $106. An independent trader was seen quoting 380-cst at $107. Bunker 180-cst was at $111-$112.</p>
<p>Supplies are in abundance, a trader said.</p>
<p>MDO and gas oil were also lower at $207-$210 and $230 down from $220-$222 and $235 respectively.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3082)</p>
